# Vulnerability details

Relevant files: [Core::deployVaults](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-karak/blob/f5e52fdcb4c20c4318d532a9f08f7876e9afb321/src/Core.sol#L161-L168), [CoreLib::deployVaults](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-karak/blob/f5e52fdcb4c20c4318d532a9f08f7876e9afb321/src/entities/CoreLib.sol#L124-L142)
### Impact
Karak protocol allows Operators to deploy special type of vault called `NativeVault`, which allows protocol users to re-stake their natively staked ether. Due to the way `NativeVault` works, it is required to receive some addresses upon initialization, namely: `manager`, `slashStore`, `nodeImplementation`. 
```js
(address manager, address slashStore, address nodeImplementation) = abi.decode(_extraData, (address, address, address));
```

The issue is that no checks are performed for these operator-supplied addresses, which opens the `NativeVault` to a multitude of issues:

1. A malicious manager can change the `NativeNode` implementation at any point. This means that the `withdraw` function can be re-written to transfer funds to attacker's address.
2. A malicious manager can pause functions in `NativeNode` and `NativeVault` making certain actions temporarily DoSed.
3. A different `slashStore` from what is registered in `Core` can be supplied, which will cause `slashAssets` function to revert. This means that to slash such `NativeVault` the assets allow list has to be temporarily updated and then brought back to normal. This puts a strain on normal protocol operations.
4. A malicious `nodeImplementation` can be supplied from the get-go with the same worst-case impact as point **1**.

### Root Cause
Arbitrary addresses are given to `NativeVault` which lack necessary checks.
### PoC
This PoC demonstrates the following impacts:
1. Supplying arbitrary `NativeNode` implementation upon `NativeVault` init
2. Malicious manager changing node implementation
3. `NativeNode` withdrawals redirecting funds to attackers' address
4. Attempts to slash will revert

Create a file `test/nativeRestaking/MaliciousNativeVault.t.sol` with the following content:
