# Vulnerability details

## Impact
While a proper way to handle fee-on-transfer tokens slashing in the `SlashingHandler`'s `handleSlashing` function would be checking the `token.balanceOf(address(this))` value after the `transferFrom` call completes, the current implementation of the `handleSlashing` function doesn't have this feature and thus will always revert and be DoS'ed to slash fee-on-transfer tokens.

**Please note that this comment was already made by Slither, but it doesn't stress enough how disasterous and impactful not implementing the proper handling for real `token.balanceOf(address(this))` is.`

The problem is that the `SlashingHandler` will attempt to transfer `amount` of `token` to the `address(0)`.

But the `amount` is actually the initial argument that the `handleSlashing` function receives, and it is the argument used to indicate how much of a `token` to transfer from the `msg.sender`.

But the real amount of `token` received may be less than the initial `amount`, if the `token` is a rebalance or a fee-on-transfer token.

And during the `SafeTransferLib.safeTransfer(address(token), address(0), amount);` call this function will always revert.

